var e=[{slug:`atlanta`,stateSlug:`georgia`,name:`Atlanta`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Atlanta`,intro:`Atlanta-based Hylton Casting and Georgia’s official film-office resources offer practical starting points for background work. Learn where to look, how to follow project instructions, and why a Georgia listing is not necessarily an Atlanta shoot.`,overview:[`For Atlanta beginners, it helps to separate a casting company from a film-office jobs page. Hylton Casting identifies Atlanta as its base; the Georgia Film Office’s professional-development page covers film and television work throughout the state.`,`The state page includes a background-actor referral to Hylton alongside production-office and crew listings. Read the job category carefully: a crew call is not an extras application, and a statewide listing does not establish where you would report. Start with the official company website for its own instructions.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Scripted-series background`,text:`Georgia’s film-office page documents a scripted-series background referral. It illustrates a type of work to research, not a promise of an available Atlanta role.`},{title:`Period-specific looks`,text:`That state-listed series describes a 1990s and early-2000s setting. Wardrobe and appearance needs belong to the individual project; do not assume all Atlanta work uses period looks.`}],beginnerTips:[`Begin at Hylton Casting’s official homepage and look for its Talent Registration information rather than using an old registration link.`,`Read the individual background notice for required photos, availability, and submission details; do not send an extras application to a crew-call contact.`,`Be honest about your measurements, availability, and transportation. Keep recent, natural photos ready.`],localConsiderations:[`Georgia’s film-office listings cover the entire state. Confirm the actual work location before assuming a listing is within metro Atlanta.`,`An Atlanta-based casting company may handle projects elsewhere; plan travel around a confirmed booking, not the company’s address.`,`The state professional-development page also includes training and crew work. Those resources are not guarantees of background roles.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Hylton Casting`,description:`Atlanta-based casting company identified on its official website and referenced by the Georgia Film Office. Use its own website for project and registration information.`,url:`https://hyltoncasting.com/`,scope:`Atlanta-based; project locations vary`,evidenceId:`hylton`},{name:`Georgia Film Office — Professional Development`,description:`Official film jobs and training information. Distinguish background notices from crew positions and check each project’s location.`,url:`https://georgia.org/industries/film/professional-development`,scope:`Statewide Georgia`,evidenceId:`georgia`}],nearby:[{name:`Savannah`,stateSlug:`georgia`,slug:`savannah`},{name:`Macon`,stateSlug:`georgia`},{name:`Charlotte`,stateSlug:`north-carolina`,slug:`charlotte`}],faqs:[{q:`Where can I start looking for Atlanta background work?`,a:`Start with Hylton Casting’s official website and the Georgia Film Office’s professional-development page. Check the role category, location, and dates in each notice before applying.`},{q:`Is the Georgia film-office jobs page Atlanta-only?`,a:`No. It covers film and television projects throughout Georgia and includes crew work as well as background information. Look for a background-specific notice and its actual work location.`},{q:`Where should I find Hylton Casting’s registration information?`,a:`Use Hylton’s official homepage and its Talent Registration information. The state film-office page refers readers there; registration or a submission does not guarantee a booking.`},{q:`Should I travel to Atlanta before I have a booking?`,a:`Treat casting as a possibility, not a travel plan. Confirm the reporting location and your ability to meet the booking requirements before making arrangements.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Atlanta?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-25`},{slug:`savannah`,stateSlug:`georgia`,name:`Savannah`,published:!0,headline:`Background Acting in Savannah`,intro:`Savannah’s regional film commission shares casting notices, but it does not cast or register background performers itself. Its local archive is a useful starting point for learning which notices concern the Savannah region and what each project asks of applicants.`,overview:[`The Savannah Regional Film Commission directs performers to casting notices in its News section and social updates. Its FAQ explicitly separates that service from casting: the commission does not act as an agency or list and promote actors, extras, or background artists.`,`Dated local notices can teach you how submissions work without being current openings. A July 2026 Savannah feature-film notice asked for recent photos, clothing sizes, and relevant experience, and specified local-hire terms. Those details belonged to that project; check the latest notice rather than reusing its old instructions.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature-film background`,text:`A July 2026 Savannah feature notice included background portrayals requiring medical experience. It is a historical example, not a current opening or a requirement for all extras.`},{title:`Skill-specific doubles`,text:`The same dated notice sought experienced tennis players for doubles. Double work can have specific skill and appearance requirements; it is not interchangeable with general background work.`}],beginnerTips:[`Check a notice’s publication date and work dates before contacting its casting team; the commission’s archive includes past projects.`,`Have current close-up and full-body photos, clothing sizes, and a truthful description of relevant skills ready. Follow the individual notice’s requirements.`,`Use the casting contact named in a suitable notice, not the film commission’s crew database, to follow performer submission instructions.`],localConsiderations:[`Check local-hire, travel, and mileage terms before planning a visit. One dated Savannah notice excluded travel and mileage; that was a project-specific condition, not a citywide rule.`,`The commission’s crew-resume database is separate from its casting information. Do not mistake a crew listing for an extras signup.`,`An archived notice is not evidence that applications remain open, even when its page is still online.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Savannah Regional Film Commission — Casting Calls`,description:`Regional casting-notice archive. Check publication dates, filming dates, and the named casting contact; older entries are not active opportunities.`,url:`https://www.filmsavannah.org/category/casting-calls/`,scope:`Savannah region`,evidenceId:`savannah-casting`},{name:`Savannah Regional Film Commission — FAQ`,description:`Explains the commission’s role, where it shares casting notices, and why its crew database is not background-performer registration.`,url:`https://www.filmsavannah.org/about-us/faq/`,scope:`Savannah region`,evidenceId:`savannah-faq`}],nearby:[{name:`Atlanta`,stateSlug:`georgia`,slug:`atlanta`},{name:`Wilmington`,stateSlug:`north-carolina`,slug:`wilmington`}],faqs:[{q:`Does the Savannah Regional Film Commission cast extras?`,a:`No. Its FAQ says it does not act as a casting agency or list and promote background performers. It shares notices so readers can follow the casting team’s instructions.`},{q:`Where does the commission share casting notices?`,a:`Its FAQ points to the website’s News section and its Facebook page. The website also has a Casting Calls archive; check dates before treating a notice as current.`},{q:`What photos should I prepare for a Savannah submission?`,a:`A dated local notice requested current close-up and full-body photos without hats, sunglasses, or other people. Prepare clear, recent photos, but follow the exact requirements of the notice you apply to.`},{q:`Can visitors assume travel expenses are covered?`,a:`No. A July 2026 Savannah notice specified local hires with no travel or mileage reimbursement. Do not apply that condition to every project; check each notice and booking’s terms.`},{q:`Is the commission’s crew database a background-actor signup?`,a:`No. Its FAQ describes a crew-resume database separately from performer casting information. For background work, follow the contact and instructions in the relevant casting notice.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-25`},{slug:`los-angeles`,stateSlug:`california`,name:`Los Angeles`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming a Background Actor in Los Angeles`,intro:`Start your Los Angeles background-acting search with Central Casting’s California roles page and its official signup guidance. Read each notice for the actual location, work dates, and requirements before applying.`,overview:[`Central Casting’s California Open Roles page includes Los Angeles-area postings, but the page’s California label is not a guarantee that every notice is nearby. Read the location, work dates, and project requirements before deciding a notice fits you; older posts may remain visible.`,`Central Casting’s Get Cast guidance explains how to sign up and prepare a profile. Use casting-company instructions for applications; the California Film Commission’s safety and child-performer work-permit resources address different needs.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Film & television background`,text:`Central Casting’s general guidance lists feature films and TV shows among the productions using its casting teams. These categories do not identify which Los Angeles projects have openings.`},{title:`Commercials & music videos`,text:`Central Casting also describes commercial and music-video work. Read each notice for its own dates, location, and role requirements.`},{title:`Skills & vehicle matching`,text:`Its profile guide explains how genuine skills, sizes, and vehicle details can help match talent to specialized needs. Do not claim equipment or experience you do not have.`}],beginnerTips:[`Use Central Casting’s official Get Cast information to understand its process; follow the requirements of an individual notice rather than assuming every role has the same prerequisites.`,`Keep current photos, accurate sizes, and contact details in your casting profile. Update the information when your appearance changes.`,`List only skills you can actually perform. Central Casting’s profile guide explains that skills and vehicle information help match performers to specific needs.`],localConsiderations:[`Check the precise location on each California posting. Do not assume Los Angeles-area labeling means the same reporting location for every project.`,`Plan your trip around the reporting address and required arrival time in your booking details, not a casting company’s office address.`,`Confirm reporting instructions with the casting or production contact before arranging travel; a publicly visible posting is not a booking.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Central Casting — California Open Roles`,description:`Official casting-company notices, including Los Angeles-area work. Check individual locations, dates, and prerequisites; no particular opening is promised here.`,url:`https://www.centralcasting.com/jobs/california/index.html`,scope:`California page; locations vary by notice`,evidenceId:`centralCA`},{name:`California Film Commission`,description:`Official on-set safety and child-performer work-permit information. For background applications, use the casting company’s instructions.`,url:`https://film.ca.gov/`,scope:`Statewide California`,evidenceId:`cfc`}],nearby:[{name:`San Francisco`,stateSlug:`california`,slug:`san-francisco`},{name:`San Diego`,stateSlug:`california`},{name:`Albuquerque`,stateSlug:`new-mexico`,slug:`albuquerque`}],faqs:[{q:`Where can I look for Los Angeles background notices?`,a:`Central Casting’s official California Open Roles page is one starting point. Read each posting’s actual location, dates, and requirements; the page also retains dated notices and is not a guarantee of available work.`},{q:`Can a beginner use Central Casting’s resources?`,a:`Central Casting’s general Get Cast guidance says no experience is required and welcomes union and non-union performers. Individual roles and signup still have their own eligibility requirements, and participation does not guarantee work.`},{q:`What should I keep current in my casting profile?`,a:`Central Casting recommends current photos, accurate sizes, contact information, and other details as they change. List only skills you are proficient in, and describe your actual vehicle if you are willing to work with it.`},{q:`Does a public filming announcement mean I can join the background?`,a:`No. Apply through the named casting company and wait for a confirmed booking. A filming announcement is not permission to visit a set.`},{q:`Is the California Film Commission a casting agency?`,a:`No. Its website provides statewide production information, including work-permit and on-set safety resources. Use an appropriate casting contact for performer applications.`},{q:`Does a California roles page mean every shoot is in Los Angeles?`,a:`No. Check the location in the individual notice. Do not make travel arrangements based on a broad page label or assume an old posting remains open.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`austin`,stateSlug:`texas`,name:`Austin`,published:!0,headline:`Background Acting in Austin`,intro:`Austin’s film commission points readers to local employment tools and Texas’s statewide Job Hotline. For a first background role, separate performer notices from crew jobs, check the filming location, and understand the submission terms before committing.`,overview:[`The Austin Film Commission’s Employment Tools page links to local casting-director directories and the Texas Film Commission Job Hotline. Its production directory is for local crew and vendors; it is not a general background-performer signup.`,`The Texas Film Commission offers a separate guide to starting as an actor and a Casting Calls board for actors, talent, and extras. The board covers all Texas, so an Austin reader should check each project’s work location rather than assuming a statewide listing is local.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Screen-production background`,text:`Austin’s employment guide points to casting resources for film, television, and commercials. Research background-specific notices; crew positions and speaking roles are different categories.`},{title:`Crowd & everyday scenes`,text:`The Texas actor guide describes background scenes such as games, parades, and restaurants. These illustrate what extras do, not current Austin openings.`}],beginnerTips:[`Use the Casting Calls category rather than a crew or technical-job listing when looking for performer work.`,`The state actor guide recommends sending recent photos and contact information to the address in the notice. Follow any additional project-specific instructions.`,`Confirm dates and compensation in a written deal memo or contract before committing. The state guide recommends written terms even for unpaid or volunteer work.`],localConsiderations:[`Use Austin’s Employment Tools page to orient yourself locally, then check the precise location and dates on a statewide Hotline notice.`,`Texas Hotline rules exclude student projects receiving course credit. The board is not a complete picture of every educational or independent project around Austin.`,`Hotline rules prohibit application and audition fees. They are the board’s rules, not a guarantee that every acting advertisement elsewhere follows them.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Austin Film Commission — Employment Tools`,description:`Local orientation to cast and crew resources, casting-director directories, and the statewide Job Hotline. Distinguish performer resources from crew listings.`,url:`https://www.austintexas.org/film-commission/resources/employment-tools/`,scope:`Austin area, with statewide links`,evidenceId:`AUSTIN_TOOLS`},{name:`Texas Film Commission — Casting Calls`,description:`Official statewide board for performer notices. Check filming locations, dates, and whether a notice is actually for background work.`,url:`https://gov.texas.gov/film/hotline/casting`,scope:`Statewide Texas`,evidenceId:`TX_CASTING`},{name:`Texas Film Commission — Getting Started as an Actor`,description:`Explains extras submissions, preparation, and written work terms, with links to Texas casting resources.`,url:`https://gov.texas.gov/film/page/filming_extras`,scope:`Statewide Texas`,evidenceId:`TX_ACTOR`}],nearby:[{name:`San Antonio`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`san-antonio`},{name:`Dallas–Fort Worth`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`dallas-fort-worth`},{name:`Houston`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`houston`}],faqs:[{q:`Where can I start looking for Austin background notices?`,a:`Use Austin Film Commission’s Employment Tools page for local orientation and the Texas Film Commission Casting Calls board for notices. The state board covers all Texas, so check locations carefully.`},{q:`How does the Texas actor guide say to submit?`,a:`Send recent photographs and contact information to the address listed in a suitable notice, following its additional instructions. The guide says a production will contact you only if you are needed for filming.`},{q:`Do I need an agent just to respond to a Hotline notice?`,a:`The state guide describes direct submissions to notices and contact with extras casting directors. Representation is discussed separately for pursuing more substantial acting roles; follow the individual notice’s requirements.`},{q:`Does the Texas Hotline include student films?`,a:`Its rules exclude projects in which participants receive course credit. Do not treat an absence from the board as proof that no educational film projects exist around Austin.`},{q:`Should a Hotline application or audition charge a fee?`,a:`No. Texas Film Commission Hotline rules prohibit application and audition fees. Be cautious if someone claiming to represent a Hotline project requests one.`},{q:`Is Austin’s production directory an extras signup?`,a:`The commission describes its production directory as a resource for local crew and vendors. Its Employment Tools page separately points to casting-director directories and casting information.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-25`},{slug:`albuquerque`,stateSlug:`new-mexico`,name:`Albuquerque`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Albuquerque`,intro:`Albuquerque’s film office has a dedicated actor resource page that separates background casting contacts from principal casting and talent agencies. Pair that local guidance with New Mexico’s statewide casting board, checking each notice’s location and dates.`,overview:[`The City of Albuquerque’s Resources for Actors page lists background casting contacts and explains how to prepare for non-speaking work. It recommends current photos, accurate measurements, reliable contact information, and following individual casting-company instructions.`,`The New Mexico Film Office’s casting board is statewide, not Albuquerque-only. Its wider Bulletin Board also includes training, crew, volunteer, and other announcements. Both the city directory and state board carry limitations on endorsement, so an official listing should not be treated as a guaranteed booking or a certification of every advertiser.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Non-speaking background`,text:`Albuquerque’s guide describes background performers who help scenes feel authentic. Role requirements depend on the particular scene and production, not a citywide performer profile.`},{title:`Principal roles & other notices`,text:`The city lists principal casting separately from background contacts; the state board also includes crew and training notices. These are related resources, not interchangeable background bookings.`}],beginnerTips:[`Prepare current full-body and chest-up photos against a plain, neutral background, as recommended by Albuquerque’s actor guide.`,`Keep accurate sizes and contact details ready, and monitor the email address you provide to casting contacts.`,`Follow each background company’s own instructions. The city says some use databases and social updates, not one universal city registration form.`],localConsiderations:[`Check the location and dates in New Mexico casting notices; statewide postings need not film in Albuquerque.`,`The city says casting companies usually request all-day availability. If you cannot meet that request or must cancel, contact the casting company promptly.`,`The city and state do not certify or endorse every directory or bulletin-board entry. Verify the contact and work terms before sharing information or committing.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Albuquerque Film Office — Resources for Actors`,description:`City-hosted background casting contacts and practical actor preparation guidance. Directory entries are not city endorsements.`,url:`https://www.cabq.gov/film/resources-for-actors`,scope:`Albuquerque area; some contacts serve wider New Mexico`,evidenceId:`ABQ_ACTOR`},{name:`New Mexico Film Office — Casting Calls`,description:`Official statewide casting notices with project dates and locations. Check each notice rather than assuming it concerns Albuquerque.`,url:`https://nmfilm.com/jobs-training/casting-calls`,scope:`Statewide New Mexico`,evidenceId:`NM_CASTING`},{name:`New Mexico Film Office — Bulletin Board`,description:`Broader casting, crew, education, and community announcements, with the state’s listing policies and endorsement limitations.`,url:`https://nmfilm.com/about-us/bulletin-board`,scope:`Statewide New Mexico`,evidenceId:`NM_RULES`}],nearby:[{name:`Santa Fe`,stateSlug:`new-mexico`,slug:`santa-fe`},{name:`Austin`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`austin`},{name:`Los Angeles`,stateSlug:`california`,slug:`los-angeles`}],faqs:[{q:`Where can I find Albuquerque background casting contacts?`,a:`Start with the city’s Resources for Actors page, which lists background casting contacts separately from principal casting and agents. It also links to New Mexico Film Office casting notices.`},{q:`What photos does the city recommend?`,a:`Current full-body and chest-up photos against a plain, neutral background that accurately show your present appearance. Keep your sizes and contact information current too.`},{q:`Should I pay to be listed with an extras casting company?`,a:`Albuquerque’s actor guidance says not to pay to be listed with an extras casting company or talent agency. Treat a request for a listing fee as a warning and check the contact independently.`},{q:`Should I keep the entire workday available?`,a:`The city says casting companies usually ask for all-day availability. Follow your actual booking requirements and contact the casting company promptly if your availability changes.`},{q:`Does an official directory entry guarantee legitimacy?`,a:`No. The city does not certify or endorse every entry, and the state says its Bulletin Board does not warrant listed companies’ or individuals’ legitimacy. Check the contact and terms independently.`},{q:`Are New Mexico casting notices all in Albuquerque?`,a:`No. The state board covers New Mexico and identifies individual locations and dates. Check those details before applying or making travel plans.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-25`},{slug:`new-york-city`,stateSlug:`new-york`,name:`New York City`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in New York City`,intro:`AND Casting’s free talent database and Atmosphere Casting’s New York resources offer starting points for background work. Check each company’s instructions and the actual reporting location before applying.`,overview:[`AND Casting describes itself as specializing in sourcing local background extras for feature films and television series, with offices in New York and New Jersey. Its talent database is free to join, and the company says it works with SAG, union, and non-union talent.`,`Atmosphere Casting lists New York City among the places where it maintains performer databases. Different companies handle different projects, so follow each company’s current registration and submission instructions. A profile is not a booking.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature-film & series background`,text:`AND Casting identifies feature films and television series as its background-casting focus. That describes the company’s services, not a list of current openings.`},{title:`Union & non-union roles`,text:`The company states it works with SAG, union, and non-union talent. Individual productions set their own eligibility requirements.`},{title:`Commercial work`,text:`AND Casting’s featured work includes commercial projects alongside features. Check each notice for its own dates, location, and requirements.`}],beginnerTips:[`Create a free profile in AND Casting’s talent database and keep your photos, sizes, and contact details current.`,`Read each notice’s reporting location carefully. A New York-area project may report anywhere in the five boroughs or across the river in New Jersey.`,`Follow the submission instructions in the individual notice rather than sending a general application to a city office.`],localConsiderations:[`The New York market spans five boroughs, and some New York-based casting companies also cast New Jersey projects. Confirm where you would actually report before accepting a booking.`,`Check your call time—the required arrival time—and whether you can reach the reporting address before committing.`,`Plan both your trip to set and your trip home. Use the confirmed booking details rather than assuming a New York-area notice fits your usual commute.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`AND Casting`,description:`Background casting company with New York and New Jersey offices and a free talent database for feature, television, and commercial work.`,url:`https://www.andcasting.com/`,scope:`New York and New Jersey`,evidenceId:`nyc-and`},{name:`Atmosphere Casting`,description:`Extras casting service that lists New York City among the major cities where it maintains performer databases.`,url:`https://atmospherecasting.org/`,scope:`National, including New York City`,evidenceId:`nyc-atmosphere`}],nearby:[{name:`Boston`,stateSlug:`massachusetts`,slug:`boston`},{name:`Pittsburgh`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`,slug:`pittsburgh`},{name:`Philadelphia`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`,slug:`philadelphia`},{name:`Buffalo`,stateSlug:`new-york`,slug:`buffalo`}],faqs:[{q:`Where can I start looking for New York City background work?`,a:`AND Casting’s free talent database is one verified starting point, and Atmosphere Casting lists New York among its database cities. Follow each company’s own registration and notice instructions.`},{q:`Is the Mayor’s Office of Media and Entertainment a casting agency?`,a:`No. It is the city’s official office for film, television, and media production. It supports and promotes production but does not cast or register background performers.`},{q:`Do I need to be in the union to work as an extra in New York?`,a:`AND Casting says it works with SAG, union, and non-union talent, so non-union beginners can register. Individual productions set their own requirements, and registration does not guarantee bookings.`},{q:`Does a New York casting company only cast New York shoots?`,a:`Not necessarily. AND Casting also has a New Jersey office, and companies may cast projects in either state. Check the reporting location in each notice.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in New York?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`chicago`,stateSlug:`illinois`,name:`Chicago`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Chicago`,intro:`Chicago’s city film office publishes background contacts for local television series and a list of casting agencies. Start with those contacts, check the latest notices, and follow the instructions for the specific project.`,overview:[`The City of Chicago Film Office’s Current Production and Casting Information page lists separate background contacts for Chicago Fire, Chicago Med, and Chicago PD, including dedicated email addresses, Facebook pages, and a mailing list that sends casting notices directly.`,`The same page lists Chicago casting agencies, including 4 Star Casting, Cine-Casting, Extra Ordinary Casting of Chicago, Joan Philo Casting, Marinella Hume Casting, and O’Connor Casting. Find each company’s current performer instructions on its own official website; a directory entry is not a booking.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Network-series background`,text:`The city page maintains background contacts for three Chicago-based NBC series. A named contact shows where notices appear, not that a role is currently open.`},{title:`Commercial & independent casting`,text:`The city’s agency list includes companies covering commercial and full-service casting. Each agency has its own registration process and project mix.`}],beginnerTips:[`Start at the city film office’s casting page and use the contact listed for the specific show you are interested in — each series handles background separately.`,`Sign up for the mailing list the city page links to so new notices reach you directly, and follow the named Facebook pages for the latest posts.`,`Keep recent photos and accurate sizes ready, and never pay a fee simply to apply for background work.`],localConsiderations:[`Series background contacts are show-specific. An email address for one production is not a general Chicago extras registration.`,`Chicago productions film across the city’s neighborhoods, so confirm the reporting location and your transportation before accepting a booking.`,`The city’s agency list is informational. Verify any company’s current process on its own official site before sharing personal information.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Chicago Film Office — Production & Casting Information`,description:`Official city page naming current series background contacts, a notice mailing list, and established local casting agencies.`,url:`https://www.chicago.gov/city/en/depts/dca/supp_info/chicago_film_office_production_casting.html`,scope:`Chicago`,evidenceId:`chi-filmoffice`}],nearby:[{name:`Milwaukee`,stateSlug:`wisconsin`},{name:`Indianapolis`,stateSlug:`indiana`}],faqs:[{q:`Where can I find Chicago background casting notices?`,a:`The City of Chicago Film Office publishes a casting-information page with the background contacts for Chicago Fire, Chicago Med, and Chicago PD, plus a mailing list for notices. Start there rather than with unofficial reposts.`},{q:`Do the Chicago series share one extras contact?`,a:`No. The city page lists separate emails and Facebook pages for each series, though Chicago Med and Chicago PD share an Instagram account and mailing list. Use the contact for the specific show.`},{q:`Does the city film office cast extras itself?`,a:`No. It publishes casting information and agency contacts as a public resource. Actual casting is handled by the productions and the casting companies they hire.`},{q:`Are the agencies on the city’s list endorsed by the city?`,a:`The page presents them as agencies that may provide additional information and opportunities. Treat the list as a starting point and verify each company’s current process independently.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Chicago?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`new-orleans`,stateSlug:`louisiana`,name:`New Orleans`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in New Orleans`,intro:`New Orleans has two established full-service casting companies with deep local roots — Caballero Casting and Coulon Casting — plus a city film office. Both companies cast background performers alongside principal roles.`,overview:[`Caballero Casting, owned by Brent Caballero, CSA, offers principal and extras casting for feature films, television shows, commercials, and music videos, with offices in New Orleans and Baton Rouge.`,`Coulon Casting casts principal actors and background extras for feature, television, and commercial productions across the Southern region. For a beginner, the useful next step is each company’s official performer instructions—not a general production directory.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature & television background`,text:`Both Caballero and Coulon describe feature and television extras casting among their services. Service descriptions are not lists of current openings.`},{title:`Commercials & music videos`,text:`Caballero Casting includes commercials and music videos in its extras work. Check each company’s current notices for actual projects.`},{title:`Regional Southern productions`,text:`Coulon Casting describes work across Louisiana, Texas, Mississippi, Alabama, Florida, and Georgia. A New Orleans company’s notice may concern a shoot elsewhere in the region.`}],beginnerTips:[`Visit each casting company’s official website to find its current registration process rather than relying on third-party reposts.`,`Because local companies also serve Baton Rouge and the wider South, check the work location in every notice before assuming it is a New Orleans shoot.`,`Prepare recent photos and accurate sizes, and follow the specific submission instructions in each notice.`],localConsiderations:[`New Orleans and Baton Rouge are separate production markets roughly 80 miles apart. A company with offices in both may cast for either.`,`Regional casting scope means a New Orleans-based company’s project could film in another state. Confirm the location before committing.`,`Keep recent photos and clothing sizes ready so you can follow a suitable notice’s requested format without rushing or guessing.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Caballero Casting`,description:`Full-service casting company with New Orleans and Baton Rouge offices, casting principal and extras roles for features, television, commercials, and music videos.`,url:`https://www.caballerocasting.com/about`,scope:`New Orleans and Baton Rouge`,evidenceId:`nola-caballero`},{name:`Coulon Casting`,description:`New Orleans casting company working since 2002 on principal and background casting for film, television, and commercials across the Southern region.`,url:`https://couloncasting.com/`,scope:`New Orleans; projects across the Southern US`,evidenceId:`nola-coulon`}],nearby:[{name:`Baton Rouge`,stateSlug:`louisiana`,slug:`baton-rouge`},{name:`Austin`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`austin`},{name:`Atlanta`,stateSlug:`georgia`,slug:`atlanta`}],faqs:[{q:`Which casting companies handle background work in New Orleans?`,a:`Caballero Casting and Coulon Casting both describe extras casting among their services and identify as New Orleans companies. Use each company’s official site for its current registration process.`},{q:`Is a New Orleans casting notice always for a New Orleans shoot?`,a:`No. Caballero also has a Baton Rouge office, and Coulon casts across several Southern states. Check the work location in each notice.`},{q:`Do I register with the city or a casting company?`,a:`Use the casting company’s official performer instructions. Film New Orleans does not register extras, and creating a casting profile does not guarantee selection.`},{q:`Do I need experience to register with a New Orleans casting company?`,a:`Background work generally does not require acting experience, but each company and project sets its own requirements. Follow the instructions on the company’s official site.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in New Orleans?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`dallas-fort-worth`,stateSlug:`texas`,name:`Dallas–Fort Worth`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Dallas–Fort Worth`,intro:`The Fort Worth Film Commission points aspiring extras to Legacy Casting’s MyCastingFile registration. Use that performer guidance and individual casting notices to research background work across Dallas–Fort Worth.`,overview:[`Legacy Casting says it is currently casting projects in Texas and Montana, with registration through the MyCastingFile database and a Dallas office phone line. The Fort Worth Film Commission recommends creating a MyCastingFile profile to view open casting calls and be considered for background roles.`,`The Fort Worth Film Commission’s FAQ explains how to get started as a background actor and points to casting opportunities on its social channels and the Texas Film Commission Job Hotline. Look for performer notices rather than crew jobs, and check the actual filming location.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Series & feature background`,text:`The Fort Worth Film Commission describes large-scale series and features filming in the metroplex and names Legacy Casting as a frequent extras source. This is context, not a list of open roles.`},{title:`Faith-based & independent production`,text:`The commission separately directs performers interested in The Chosen to Brock Allen Casting. Individual productions may use their own casting companies.`},{title:`Statewide Texas notices`,text:`The Texas Film Commission’s Casting Calls board covers the whole state. Check each notice’s filming location rather than assuming a DFW shoot.`}],beginnerTips:[`Create a profile on MyCastingFile, the database Legacy Casting uses for registration and project notices.`,`Follow the Fort Worth Film Commission’s social channels, where it posts local casting opportunities, and check the Texas Film Commission’s statewide board.`,`Read each notice’s location, dates, and submission instructions; a Texas-wide listing is not automatically a Dallas–Fort Worth job.`],localConsiderations:[`Dallas and Fort Worth are about 30 miles apart, and productions film across the metroplex. Confirm the actual reporting location before accepting a booking.`,`Legacy Casting also casts projects in Montana, so check that a notice concerns a Texas production.`,`Some productions hire their own casting companies — The Chosen, for example, works with Brock Allen Casting rather than the usual local channel.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Legacy Casting — Registration`,description:`Extras casting company for Texas projects, registering performers through the MyCastingFile database. Recommended by the Fort Worth Film Commission for DFW background work.`,url:`https://legacycasting.com/register/`,scope:`Dallas–Fort Worth and other Texas locations; also casts Montana projects`,evidenceId:`dfw-legacy`},{name:`Fort Worth Film Commission`,description:`City film commission whose FAQ answers how to work as a background actor in Fort Worth and shares casting opportunities on social media.`,url:`https://www.fortworth.com/film/`,scope:`Fort Worth and the wider metroplex`,evidenceId:`dfw-fortworth`},{name:`Texas Film Commission — Casting Calls`,description:`Official statewide board for performer notices. Check filming locations and dates on each listing.`,url:`https://gov.texas.gov/film/hotline/casting`,scope:`Statewide Texas`,evidenceId:`TX_CASTING`}],nearby:[{name:`Austin`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`austin`},{name:`Houston`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`houston`},{name:`San Antonio`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`san-antonio`}],faqs:[{q:`How do I register for background work in Dallas–Fort Worth?`,a:`The Fort Worth Film Commission recommends creating a profile at MyCastingFile, the database Legacy Casting uses, to view open casting calls and be considered for background roles.`},{q:`Are Dallas and Fort Worth the same market for extras?`,a:`They function as one large production region — the commissions and casting companies serve the wider metroplex — but the two downtowns are about 30 miles apart. Always confirm the reporting location in your booking.`},{q:`Do the film commissions cast extras?`,a:`No. The Dallas and Fort Worth commissions support production and share information; the Fort Worth commission’s FAQ directs background performers to Legacy Casting’s registration instead.`},{q:`Does every DFW production use the same casting company?`,a:`No. The Fort Worth Film Commission notes that many large-scale productions work with Legacy Casting, but it separately points performers for The Chosen to Brock Allen Casting. Check each production’s own instructions.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Dallas–Fort Worth?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`wilmington`,stateSlug:`north-carolina`,name:`Wilmington`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Wilmington`,intro:`Wilmington’s background work runs through TW Cast & Recruit’s CastGen extras database, and the North Carolina Film Office’s official list of recently wrapped productions shows steady feature and series activity in the Wilmington region.`,overview:[`TW Cast & Recruit uses its CastGen database for extras casting: you build a profile with current contact information, a headshot, and a full-body photo; choose the projects and roles you are available for; and confirm booking requests by text message.`,`The North Carolina Film Office publishes a list of productions that have wrapped within the last 18 months, and its 2025–2026 entries include several Wilmington Region features and series, among them Drivers Ed, Pretty/Ugly, A Proper Christmas, and the RJ Decker pilot and first season. Wrapped productions prove the region attracts work; they are not current openings.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature-film background`,text:`The state film office’s recent-wraps list includes multiple feature films shot in the Wilmington Region in 2025 and 2026. Historical wraps do not indicate current casting.`},{title:`Series background`,text:`The same list records the RJ Decker pilot and first season filming in the Wilmington Region. Series work can recur, but each season casts separately.`},{title:`Large-scale event production`,text:`Beast Games filmed its second season in the Eastern and Wilmington Regions, according to the state list. Large productions may have unusual role and availability requirements.`}],beginnerTips:[`Build a complete CastGen profile with up-to-date contact information, a headshot, and a full-body shot — TW Cast & Recruit says this is the most current way to see available roles.`,`Respond promptly to booking-request texts; the company confirms or releases you based on your reply.`,`Follow TW Cast & Recruit on Facebook, where it posts its most recent extras calls.`],localConsiderations:[`Wilmington is a coastal city, and region-labeled productions may film outside the city itself. Check the reporting location in each booking.`,`Charlotte is a separate North Carolina production market with its own activity; do not assume a state listing concerns Wilmington.`,`The state’s recent-productions list documents completed work. Treat it as evidence of an active region, not as a casting board.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`TW Cast & Recruit — Extras Casting Calls`,description:`Wilmington-area extras casting through the CastGen database, with booking requests confirmed by text and recent calls posted on Facebook.`,url:`https://www.twcastandrecruit.com/extras-casting-calls`,scope:`Wilmington region`,evidenceId:`wil-tw`},{name:`North Carolina Film Office — Recent Productions`,description:`Official list of productions wrapped within the last 18 months, organized by region. Useful context for the Wilmington market; not a casting board.`,url:`https://www.filmnc.com/recent-productions`,scope:`Statewide, with Wilmington Region entries`,evidenceId:`wil-filmnc`}],nearby:[{name:`Charlotte`,stateSlug:`north-carolina`,slug:`charlotte`},{name:`Savannah`,stateSlug:`georgia`,slug:`savannah`},{name:`Atlanta`,stateSlug:`georgia`,slug:`atlanta`}],faqs:[{q:`How do I sign up for Wilmington extras work?`,a:`TW Cast & Recruit directs performers to its CastGen database. Create a profile with current contact information, a headshot, and a full-body photo, then mark the projects and roles you are available for.`},{q:`How will I know if I am booked?`,a:`TW Cast & Recruit describes a text-message workflow: you receive a booking request to confirm your availability, and a second message when you are officially booked.`},{q:`Is Wilmington still an active filming area?`,a:`The North Carolina Film Office’s list of productions wrapped within the last 18 months includes several 2025–2026 Wilmington Region features and series. That shows recent activity, not guaranteed future casting.`},{q:`Are Wilmington and Charlotte the same market?`,a:`No. They are separate production regions on the state film office’s list, several hours apart by car. Check which region a notice concerns.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Wilmington?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-25`},{slug:`pittsburgh`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`,name:`Pittsburgh`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Pittsburgh`,intro:`Pittsburgh’s background scene runs through the Pittsburgh Film Office’s casting notices and local companies such as Movie Casting PGH, which recruits background performers for Pittsburgh production units, including the Pittsburgh unit of The Pitt.`,overview:[`Movie Casting PGH maintains current-project pages — including an application page for The Pitt’s Pittsburgh unit — alongside background-talent explainers and FAQs for newcomers.`,`The Pittsburgh Film Office publishes regional casting notices and a directory of casting and talent agencies. Look for background-specific notices and follow the named company’s application instructions. Statewide Pennsylvania notices may concern work far from Pittsburgh.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Series background`,text:`Movie Casting PGH lists The Pitt’s Pittsburgh unit among its current projects with a dedicated application page. A listed project is not a promise of available roles.`},{title:`Feature-film background`,text:`Local press documented a 2025 feature recruiting Pittsburgh-area extras. Dated recruitment stories are historical examples, not open calls.`},{title:`Regional western Pennsylvania work`,text:`The film office’s notices and agency directory cover the wider region. Check each listing’s location and dates.`}],beginnerTips:[`Start with the Pittsburgh Film Office’s casting-notices page and its casting and talent agency directory to see who is casting locally.`,`Read Movie Casting PGH’s background-talent FAQ before applying so you understand what productions expect from extras.`,`Apply through the specific project page or notice rather than sending general availability messages.`],localConsiderations:[`Pittsburgh and Philadelphia are separate markets on opposite sides of Pennsylvania. Check the reporting location and travel time before applying or accepting a booking.`,`Dated news stories about extras recruitment describe past projects. Look for a current notice or application page before assuming a production is still hiring.`,`The film office’s directories are informational listings; verify each company’s process on its own official site.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Pittsburgh Film Office — Casting Notices`,description:`Regional film office hosting casting notices, job listings, and a directory of casting and talent agencies.`,url:`https://pghfilm.org/casting-notices/`,scope:`Pittsburgh and western Pennsylvania`,evidenceId:`pgh-filmoffice`},{name:`Movie Casting PGH`,description:`Local background casting company with current-project application pages and newcomer FAQs for Pittsburgh-area extras.`,url:`https://movieextraspittsburgh.com/`,scope:`Pittsburgh area`,evidenceId:`pgh-movieextras`}],nearby:[{name:`Philadelphia`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`,slug:`philadelphia`},{name:`New York City`,stateSlug:`new-york`,slug:`new-york-city`},{name:`Cleveland`,stateSlug:`ohio`,slug:`cleveland`}],faqs:[{q:`Where can I find Pittsburgh background casting notices?`,a:`The Pittsburgh Film Office hosts a casting-notices page and a directory of casting and talent agencies. Movie Casting PGH also posts current projects with their own application pages.`},{q:`Is The Pitt filmed in Pittsburgh?`,a:`Movie Casting PGH maintains an application page for The Pitt’s Pittsburgh unit. Production arrangements can change, so rely on the company’s current project pages rather than older articles.`},{q:`Does the Pittsburgh Film Office cast extras?`,a:`No. It publishes notices and directories as a regional resource. Casting decisions and registration belong to the casting companies and productions.`},{q:`Are Pittsburgh and Philadelphia the same market?`,a:`No. They are on opposite sides of Pennsylvania and have separate production communities. Check which city a statewide notice actually concerns.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Pittsburgh?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`boston`,stateSlug:`massachusetts`,name:`Boston`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Boston`,intro:`Boston Casting has a dedicated extras casting department and performer database for New England projects. Start with its official registration instructions, prepare current photos and sizes, and check where each project would require you to report.`,overview:[`Boston Casting describes background casting for feature films, television series, commercials, and corporate and web video. Its performer database is a way to make your details available for consideration, not a promise of auditions or bookings.`,`Use Boston Casting’s official website for its registration process and current notices. Follow the requirements of the company and individual project rather than treating a state production directory as an extras signup.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature & series background`,text:`Boston Casting lists feature films and television series among its background-casting work. Its service list is not a list of current openings.`},{title:`Commercials & corporate video`,text:`The company also casts commercials, corporate videos, and web videos. Each project sets its own requirements.`},{title:`Specialty background`,text:`Boston Casting’s database includes children, special-ability talent, and vintage cars. Specialty categories have their own eligibility rules.`}],beginnerTips:[`Register in Boston Casting’s database and keep your photos, sizes, and contact information current.`,`Watch the company’s official site and channels for casting notices rather than relying on reposts in community groups.`,`Submit only when you can meet the stated location and work dates; a New England casting company may work beyond Boston.`],localConsiderations:[`Boston Casting serves all of New England, so a booking through a Boston company may report outside the city — confirm the location before committing.`,`Massachusetts productions film statewide, from Boston neighborhoods to coastal towns. A state-level notice is not necessarily a Boston shoot.`,`Check whether the booking expects you to work as a local hire, meaning you arrange your own travel and lodging unless other terms are agreed. Confirm those terms before spending money.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Boston Casting`,description:`New England’s largest casting company, with an extras casting department and a performer database spanning features, television, and commercials.`,url:`https://www.bostoncasting.com/`,scope:`Boston and New England`,evidenceId:`bos-bostoncasting`}],nearby:[{name:`Providence`,stateSlug:`rhode-island`},{name:`New York City`,stateSlug:`new-york`,slug:`new-york-city`}],faqs:[{q:`Where do I register for Boston background work?`,a:`Boston Casting maintains a large performer database and an extras casting department. Register through its official website and keep your profile current.`},{q:`Does Boston Casting only cast Boston shoots?`,a:`No. It describes itself as the largest casting company in New England, so its projects can be elsewhere in the region. Check the reporting location in each booking.`},{q:`Where should I send a Boston extras application?`,a:`Follow Boston Casting’s official registration instructions or the contact in a suitable project notice. A state crew directory is not a background-performer application.`},{q:`Do I need experience or an agent to be an extra in Boston?`,a:`Background work generally does not require acting experience, and Boston Casting’s database includes union and non-union performers. Individual projects set their own requirements.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Boston?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`santa-fe`,stateSlug:`new-mexico`,name:`Santa Fe`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Santa Fe`,intro:`The Santa Fe Film Office maintains a dedicated page listing the background casting directors who serve northern New Mexico, and the New Mexico Film Office’s statewide casting board rounds out the picture for this distinct high-desert market.`,overview:[`The Santa Fe Film Office’s Casting Directors, Background, and P.A.’s page lists background casting directors serving the region — including Alessi/Hartigan, On Location Casting, Latham Casting, White Turtle Casting, and New Mexico Casting — alongside principal casting directors and talent agents.`,`Background contacts, principal casting directors, and talent agents serve different purposes. For non-speaking work, start with the background contacts and each company’s own performer instructions. The New Mexico Film Office’s casting board is statewide, so check whether a notice concerns Santa Fe or another location.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature & television background`,text:`The film office’s background-director list exists to serve productions filming in the region. A directory listing is not a list of current openings.`},{title:`Roles with specific requirements`,text:`Some notices request a particular appearance, background, or skill. Describe yourself truthfully and follow the individual notice’s requirements; do not assume every background role asks for the same experience.`},{title:`Statewide New Mexico notices`,text:`The state casting board covers all of New Mexico. Santa Fe and Albuquerque are separate markets about an hour apart.`}],beginnerTips:[`Use the Santa Fe Film Office’s background casting director list to find each company’s own website and registration process.`,`Check the New Mexico Film Office’s casting board for statewide notices, and confirm the work location before applying.`,`Keep current photos and accurate sizes ready, and follow the individual casting company’s instructions.`],localConsiderations:[`Santa Fe and Albuquerque are separate production markets roughly 65 miles apart. A New Mexico notice may report in either city — or somewhere else entirely.`,`The film office’s list is a directory of who works in the region. Verify each company’s current process on its own site before sharing personal information.`,`Northern New Mexico’s high-desert locations can be remote; confirm transportation and reporting details before accepting a booking.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Santa Fe Film Office — Casting Directors, Background, and P.A.’s`,description:`Official city page listing the background casting directors, principal casting directors, and talent agents serving northern New Mexico.`,url:`https://santafenm.film/actors-crew/casting-background-pa/`,scope:`Santa Fe and northern New Mexico`,evidenceId:`sf-filmoffice`},{name:`On Location Casting`,description:`Regional casting company listed by the Santa Fe Film Office, with online talent registration and performer guides covering booking, set expectations, and payment.`,url:`https://onlocationcasting.us/talent/`,scope:`Regional, including New Mexico`,evidenceId:`sf-olc`},{name:`New Mexico Film Office — Casting Calls`,description:`Official statewide casting notices with project dates and locations. Check whether a notice concerns Santa Fe.`,url:`https://nmfilm.com/jobs-training/casting-calls`,scope:`Statewide New Mexico`,evidenceId:`NM_CASTING`}],nearby:[{name:`Albuquerque`,stateSlug:`new-mexico`,slug:`albuquerque`},{name:`Las Cruces`,stateSlug:`new-mexico`}],faqs:[{q:`Who casts background performers in Santa Fe?`,a:`The Santa Fe Film Office lists background casting directors serving the region, including Alessi/Hartigan, On Location Casting, Latham Casting, White Turtle Casting, and New Mexico Casting. Register through each company’s own site.`},{q:`Are Santa Fe and Albuquerque the same market?`,a:`No. They are separate production centers about 65 miles apart. Some casting companies serve both, but always confirm which city a notice concerns.`},{q:`Does the Santa Fe Film Office register extras?`,a:`No. It publishes the directory of casting directors and talent agents as a resource. Registration happens with the individual casting companies.`},{q:`How should I use Santa Fe’s casting directory?`,a:`Start with the contacts listed for background work, then find each company’s current registration or submission instructions. Principal casting and talent-agent listings are separate paths, and none guarantees a booking.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Santa Fe?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`seattle`,stateSlug:`washington`,name:`Seattle`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Seattle`,intro:`The Northwest Film Forum’s extras casting directory points beginners to companies serving Seattle and the Pacific Northwest, including Anchor Background and Foreground Background. Use each company’s own instructions to register or respond to a suitable notice.`,overview:[`The Northwest Film Forum's extras casting directory lists the companies that handle background work in the Seattle area, including Foreground Background and Big Fish NW Talent's background division, Anchor Background. SAG-AFTRA's Seattle local also publishes a list of casting directors working in the market.`,`Anchor Background and Foreground Background describe work across the Pacific Northwest. Check the role type, dates, and reporting location on each notice; a regional database can include work beyond Seattle.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Commercial and corporate background`,text:`Anchor Background describes booking extras for commercial, film, corporate, internet, and television projects across the Pacific Northwest. Commercial work is a recurring category in this market.`},{title:`Film and television background`,text:`Foreground Background describes 15 years casting background, principals, and real people for film, television, commercials, and new media in the Pacific Northwest. Individual projects set their own needs.`},{title:`Regional background notices`,text:`Some Seattle-area companies also serve Spokane and the wider Pacific Northwest. Apply only when the actual reporting location and dates fit your transportation and availability.`}],beginnerTips:[`Start with the Northwest Film Forum's extras casting list to identify the established companies, then register through each company's own website.`,`Anchor Background is the background division of Big Fish NW Talent; read its project information and registration pages rather than calling for individual bookings.`,`Keep recent, natural photos and accurate sizes ready, and follow each notice's submission instructions exactly.`],localConsiderations:[`Seattle and Spokane are separate production areas on opposite sides of the state. Some companies serve both, but confirm where a project actually films.`,`A Washington notice may report hours from Seattle. Check travel time, parking, and any local-hire requirements before accepting.`,`Directory listings — including SAG-AFTRA's and the Northwest Film Forum's — identify who works in the market; they are not lists of current openings.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Northwest Film Forum — Extras Casting Directory`,description:`Nonprofit film organization's list of extras casting companies serving Seattle, with contact details for each.`,url:`https://nwfilm.com/talent/extras-casting/`,scope:`Seattle and the Pacific Northwest`,evidenceId:`sea-nwfilm`},{name:`Anchor Background`,description:`Background talent agency and division of Big Fish NW Talent, booking extras for commercial, film, corporate, and television projects across the Pacific Northwest.`,url:`https://anchorbackground.com/`,scope:`Seattle, Spokane, and the Pacific Northwest`,evidenceId:`sea-anchor`},{name:`Foreground Background`,description:`Seattle-area casting company with 15 years of experience casting background, principals, and real people for film, television, and commercials.`,url:`https://foregroundbackground.org/`,scope:`Seattle and the Pacific Northwest`,evidenceId:`sea-foreground`}],nearby:[{name:`Portland`,stateSlug:`oregon`,slug:`portland`},{name:`Spokane`,stateSlug:`washington`},{name:`Vancouver, BC`,stateSlug:`washington`}],faqs:[{q:`Who casts background performers in Seattle?`,a:`The Northwest Film Forum's extras casting directory lists the established companies, including Anchor Background and Foreground Background. Register through each company's own website.`},{q:`Where do I register for Seattle background work?`,a:`Follow the performer instructions on Anchor Background’s or Foreground Background’s official website. The Northwest Film Forum directory helps you identify companies, but it does not register or book you.`},{q:`Is the Northwest Film Forum a casting company?`,a:`No. It is a nonprofit film arts organization that publishes a directory of extras casting companies as a community resource.`},{q:`Do Seattle casting companies also cast in Spokane?`,a:`Some do — Anchor Background and Big Fish NW Talent describe serving both markets. Always confirm the actual reporting location in each notice.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Seattle?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`nashville`,stateSlug:`tennessee`,name:`Nashville`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Nashville`,intro:`Nashville's music and television industries create a distinctive mix of background work — from scripted series to music videos and live-audience shows. Jenny Alison Casting handles scripted background, and Audience Company Nashville casts crowds and audiences.`,overview:[`Jenny Alison Casting is based in Nashville and specializes in background casting for scripted TV and film, along with brand campaigns and TV audiences. Its FAQ page explains a submission-driven process: talent responds to individual casting calls rather than waiting for the company to check availability.`,`Audience Company Nashville describes casting extras, audiences, and crowds for music videos, feature films, talk shows, commercials, award shows, and live events. Read the role description carefully: being in an audience is different from performing as background in a scene.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Scripted TV and film background`,text:`Jenny Alison Casting describes background casting for scripted television and film as its core work. Casting calls are posted individually with their own instructions.`},{title:`Music videos and live events`,text:`Audience Company Nashville lists music videos, award shows, and live events among its casting work — a category tied closely to Nashville's music industry.`},{title:`TV audiences`,text:`Both companies describe audience casting for talk shows and live performances. Audience work has its own expectations and is not the same as background acting.`}],beginnerTips:[`Follow Jenny Alison Casting's casting calls and submit to each one individually with the requested information — the company asks talent to submit per call rather than relying on its database.`,`Read submission instructions carefully and completely; casting companies routinely discard incomplete submissions.`,`Keep recent, unfiltered photos ready, and be accurate about your availability before you submit.`],localConsiderations:[`Check whether a notice is for background acting, a live audience, or an event crowd. Each may have different arrival instructions and time commitments.`,`Some Nashville-based companies cast in other cities too — Jenny Alison Casting lists several markets. Confirm where a project actually films.`,`Apply only when you can meet the exact dates and reporting time. A Tennessee notice may concern work outside Nashville.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Jenny Alison Casting`,description:`Nashville-based company specializing in background casting for scripted TV and film, brand campaigns, and TV audiences, with a public FAQ for first-time background actors.`,url:`https://www.jennyalisoncasting.com/`,scope:`Nashville-based; casts in several markets`,evidenceId:`nsh-jennyalison`},{name:`Audience Company Nashville`,description:`Casts background extras, audiences, and crowds for music videos, feature films, talk shows, commercials, award shows, and live events in the Nashville area.`,url:`https://www.audconashville.com/aboutus`,scope:`Nashville and surrounding areas`,evidenceId:`nsh-audco`}],nearby:[{name:`Atlanta`,stateSlug:`georgia`,slug:`atlanta`},{name:`Memphis`,stateSlug:`tennessee`},{name:`Knoxville`,stateSlug:`tennessee`}],faqs:[{q:`Who casts background actors in Nashville?`,a:`Jenny Alison Casting handles scripted TV and film background, and Audience Company Nashville casts extras, audiences, and crowds for music videos, shows, and events. Apply through each company's own process.`},{q:`Do I need experience to be an extra in Nashville?`,a:`No. Jenny Alison Casting's FAQ says first-timers are welcome, though on-set experience can help in some situations. Professionalism and following instructions matter most.`},{q:`How do Nashville casting calls work?`,a:`Jenny Alison Casting asks talent to submit to each individual casting call with the requested details rather than waiting to be contacted from a database. Read and follow each call's instructions exactly.`},{q:`Is audience work the same as background acting?`,a:`No. Audience members attend tapings and live events as spectators; background actors perform in scenes. Nashville offers both, often through different companies.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Nashville?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`buffalo`,stateSlug:`new-york`,name:`Buffalo`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Buffalo`,intro:`Casting Buffalo and Buffalo Film Casting offer starting points for film, television, and commercial casting in Western New York. Follow each company’s performer instructions and check whether a notice is for background work in a location you can reach.`,overview:[`Casting Buffalo describes film, television, and commercial casting in Western New York. Buffalo Film Casting also describes principal and extras casting; different projects may use different companies, so check both official sites for their current instructions.`,`Local news has documented extras calls for holiday movies filming around Buffalo. Treat those stories as dated examples, not open calls. Use the casting company’s original notice to confirm current dates, application instructions, and pay terms.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Holiday and family features`,text:`Buffalo Film Casting lists numerous Great American Family holiday features among its credits, and local news has covered extras calls for Hallmark productions filming in the area. This is a recurring production category, not a standing opening.`},{title:`Commercials and regional campaigns`,text:`Both companies describe commercial casting among their services, including national-brand spots filmed in Western New York.`},{title:`Independent and union features`,text:`Casting Buffalo offers union (SAG-AFTRA/Equity) and non-union casting for speaking and non-speaking roles. Individual projects set their own requirements.`}],beginnerTips:[`Join the networks of both local companies — Casting Buffalo and Buffalo Film Casting — since different productions use different casting directors.`,`Watch the companies’ official channels for dated extras notices. Verify any news story or repost against the original casting company before submitting.`,`Have recent photos, basic measurements, and your real availability ready. Follow each notice’s requirements rather than assuming every holiday feature uses the same process.`],localConsiderations:[`Buffalo's production volume is seasonal and project-driven. A busy stretch of holiday features does not mean year-round work.`,`Western New York weather is a real factor: winter productions may involve long outdoor days. Confirm wardrobe and conditions before accepting.`,`Buffalo is roughly 370 miles from New York City. Downstate casting resources generally do not apply to Western New York work.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Casting Buffalo`,description:`Western New York casting company for film, television, and commercials, with union and non-union performer casting.`,url:`https://www.castingbuffalo.com/`,scope:`Buffalo and Western New York`,evidenceId:`buf-castingbuffalo`},{name:`Buffalo Film Casting`,description:`Long-running Buffalo casting company for principals and extras, with credits including numerous Great American Family features and regional commercials.`,url:`https://www.buffalofilmcasting.com/`,scope:`Buffalo and Western New York`,evidenceId:`buf-bfc`},{name:`Buffalo Niagara Film Commission — Production Directory`,description:`Official regional film commission directory of local production professionals, services, and talent.`,url:`https://www.filmbuffaloniagara.com/production-directory/`,scope:`Buffalo Niagara region`,evidenceId:`buf-bnfc`}],nearby:[{name:`Pittsburgh`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`,slug:`pittsburgh`},{name:`Cleveland`,stateSlug:`ohio`,slug:`cleveland`},{name:`New York City`,stateSlug:`new-york`,slug:`new-york-city`}],faqs:[{q:`Who casts extras in Buffalo?`,a:`Casting Buffalo and Buffalo Film Casting describe casting services in Western New York. Different productions use different companies, so follow each company’s current performer instructions.`},{q:`What kind of productions film in Buffalo?`,a:`Holiday and family features have been a recurring category — local casting companies list numerous Great American Family films, and news coverage has documented Hallmark productions casting extras in the area. Commercials and independent features also film locally.`},{q:`Is the Buffalo Niagara Film Commission a casting agency?`,a:`No. It is the regional film office; its production directory lists local professionals and services. Casting happens through the individual casting companies.`},{q:`Do Buffalo productions pay extras?`,a:`Published casting calls for recent Buffalo features listed paid background rates, with separate union and non-union rates. Rates are set per production — always read the specific call.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Buffalo?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`san-francisco`,stateSlug:`california`,name:`San Francisco`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in San Francisco`,intro:`Beau Bonneau Casting, Nancy Hayes Casting, and SAG-AFTRA’s Northern California casting directory offer starting points for Bay Area performers. Check each company’s own instructions and where a project would require you to report.`,overview:[`Beau Bonneau Casting describes more than 20 years of casting in the San Francisco Bay Area, including location and extras casting for film and television, with talent registering through Casting Networks. Nancy Hayes Casting is a full-service San Francisco agency working on projects of all sizes.`,`SAG-AFTRA’s Northern California casting page lists directors working across the Bay Area and Sacramento. Use it to identify contacts, then verify each company’s current performer process. Regional directory entries are not endorsements or confirmed openings.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Film and television extras`,text:`Beau Bonneau Casting lists location and extras casting for film and television among its services. Bay Area feature and series work ebbs and flows with production schedules.`},{title:`Commercials and corporate projects`,text:`Local casting companies describe commercial, corporate-video, and print work alongside screen roles. Check whether a notice seeks background performers, speaking actors, or another type of talent.`},{title:`Real-people casting`,text:`Several San Francisco companies specialize in casting real people rather than actors for commercials and campaigns — a distinct category with its own submission process.`}],beginnerTips:[`Beau Bonneau Casting asks talent to register and create a profile through Casting Networks for principal and extras work — start there rather than emailing headshots.`,`Use SAG-AFTRA's Northern California casting list to identify established casting directors, then follow each one's own registration process.`,`Keep your appearance, photos, and sizes current in your profiles so a casting team can assess the real you for a suitable role.`],localConsiderations:[`The Bay Area market spans nine counties. A 'San Francisco' casting may report in Oakland, San Jose, or elsewhere — confirm the location.`,`Confirm parking or transit directions and the required arrival time before accepting a booking across the Bay Area.`,`Northern California is a separate market from Los Angeles. LA casting notices generally do not apply to Bay Area talent.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Beau Bonneau Casting`,description:`Full-service Bay Area casting agency with 20-plus years of experience, including extras casting for film and television; talent registers through Casting Networks.`,url:`https://beaubonneaucasting.com/`,scope:`San Francisco Bay Area`,evidenceId:`sfo-beaubonneau`},{name:`Nancy Hayes Casting`,description:`Full-service San Francisco casting agency working on projects of all sizes.`,url:`https://www.hayescasting.com/`,scope:`San Francisco Bay Area`,evidenceId:`sfo-hayes`},{name:`SAG-AFTRA — Casting in Northern California`,description:`Union-published list of casting directors working in Northern California, from San Francisco to Sacramento.`,url:`https://www.sagaftra.org/casting-northern-california`,scope:`Northern California`,evidenceId:`sfo-sagaftra`}],nearby:[{name:`Los Angeles`,stateSlug:`california`,slug:`los-angeles`},{name:`Sacramento`,stateSlug:`california`},{name:`Portland`,stateSlug:`oregon`,slug:`portland`}],faqs:[{q:`Who casts extras in San Francisco?`,a:`Beau Bonneau Casting handles extras casting for film and television in the Bay Area, and SAG-AFTRA's Northern California page lists more than a dozen casting directors working in the region.`},{q:`How do I register for Bay Area background work?`,a:`Beau Bonneau Casting directs talent to register through Casting Networks. Other companies have their own processes — check each casting director's website.`},{q:`Does a casting directory guarantee a company or job?`,a:`No. A directory helps you find contacts, but you should verify the company’s official website, application process, and work terms before sharing personal information.`},{q:`Is Bay Area casting connected to Los Angeles?`,a:`They are separate markets with separate casting communities. Some companies work in both, but a Los Angeles notice usually requires working as a local in Southern California.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in San Francisco?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`cleveland`,stateSlug:`ohio`,name:`Cleveland`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Cleveland`,intro:`The Greater Cleveland Film Commission runs one of the most beginner-friendly setups of any market: a public casting-agencies page, a getting-started guide for new background actors, and an industry-opportunities board where local casting calls are posted.`,overview:[`The Greater Cleveland Film Commission's casting agencies page lists the local companies that cast everything from starring roles to background actors, including Angela Boehm Casting, Nancy Mosser Casting, and several others. Its getting-started page points new background actors to those agencies and to its job opportunities board.`,`The commission also publishes scam warnings for Northeast Ohio actors. Read those warnings before responding to an unexpected offer, and compare the sender’s details with the casting company’s official channels.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature film background`,text:`The commission's industry-opportunities board has carried paid extras calls for feature films shooting in Northeast Ohio. Each call names its casting company, dates, and pay rate.`},{title:`Commercials and music videos`,text:`Commission postings have included commercial stand-in and music-video casting. A stand-in helps the crew prepare lighting and camera setups and may need specific measurements or experience; read each notice rather than assuming it is general extras work.`},{title:`Regional Ohio notices`,text:`Cleveland, Columbus, and Cincinnati are separate places to search. Confirm the reporting location and whether you can meet the dates before responding to a statewide notice.`}],beginnerTips:[`Start with the Greater Cleveland Film Commission's getting-started page, which walks new background actors through the local landscape.`,`Bookmark the commission's industry-opportunities board — local casting calls are posted there with the casting company's contact details.`,`Read the commission's scam warnings before paying anyone; legitimate casting companies do not charge talent to be considered for a specific booking.`],localConsiderations:[`Northeast Ohio casting is concentrated around Cleveland, but productions film across the region — confirm whether a call is Cleveland-area or elsewhere in the state.`,`The commission warns about 'glam scams' and fake production companies targeting local actors. Verify any unexpected offer against the commission's postings.`,`Check the original notice’s date and work dates. An older casting announcement is not evidence that applications are still open.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Greater Cleveland Film Commission — Casting Agencies`,description:`Official list of local casting agencies for roles from principals to background actors, with contact details and scam-safety guidance.`,url:`https://www.clevelandfilm.com/film-here/casting-agencies`,scope:`Cleveland and Northeast Ohio`,evidenceId:`cle-gcfc`},{name:`Greater Cleveland Film Commission — Industry Opportunities`,description:`Public board where local casting calls, crew openings, and industry opportunities are posted.`,url:`https://www.clevelandfilm.com/work-here/industry-opportunities`,scope:`Northeast Ohio`,evidenceId:`cle-gcfc-jobs`},{name:`Angela Boehm Casting`,description:`Cleveland casting company handling principal, extras, real-people, and commercial casting, with recent feature-film extras calls.`,url:`https://angelaboehmcasting.com/`,scope:`Cleveland and Northeast Ohio`,evidenceId:`cle-boehm`}],nearby:[{name:`Pittsburgh`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`,slug:`pittsburgh`},{name:`Buffalo`,stateSlug:`new-york`,slug:`buffalo`},{name:`Columbus`,stateSlug:`ohio`},{name:`Detroit`,stateSlug:`michigan`,slug:`detroit`}],faqs:[{q:`How do I find Cleveland casting calls?`,a:`The Greater Cleveland Film Commission posts local casting calls on its industry-opportunities board and lists the region's casting agencies on its casting page. Both are free public resources.`},{q:`Who casts background actors in Cleveland?`,a:`The film commission's list includes Angela Boehm Casting, Nancy Mosser Casting, and several other local companies. Each casting call names the company handling it.`},{q:`Are there casting scams in Cleveland?`,a:`The Greater Cleveland Film Commission publishes warnings about scams targeting Northeast Ohio actors, including fake agencies and fraudulent production checks. Never pay to be considered for a specific role, and verify offers against the commission's postings.`},{q:`Should I apply to every Ohio notice?`,a:`Apply only when the role, location, dates, and stated requirements fit you. A statewide notice is not necessarily Cleveland-area work, and submitting does not guarantee selection.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Cleveland?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`baton-rouge`,stateSlug:`louisiana`,name:`Baton Rouge`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Baton Rouge`,intro:`Louisiana's capital has its own film commission with a dedicated 'Be an Extra' page listing the casting companies that serve the region — and Celtic Studios has anchored feature production here for years.`,overview:[`The Baton Rouge Film Commission's 'Be an Extra' page is direct about its role: the commission does not cast, but it lists the local casting companies to contact — My Casting File, Caballero Casting, Coulon Casting, and Central Casting. Caballero Casting maintains offices in both New Orleans and Baton Rouge.`,`Local news coverage documents the pattern: when a feature sets up at Celtic Studios or around the capital region, a casting company puts out a public call for local background actors with submission instructions and published pay rates. Recent coverage described a Viola Davis-led feature casting paid background through Caballero Casting.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature film background`,text:`Baton Rouge's stage facilities and locations have hosted features for decades, and local news documents recurring paid background calls when productions are in town. Work is project-driven, not continuous.`},{title:`Television and commercials`,text:`Caballero Casting describes principal and extras casting for feature films, television shows, commercials, and music videos from its Baton Rouge and New Orleans offices.`},{title:`Regional Louisiana notices`,text:`Baton Rouge and New Orleans are separate markets about 80 miles apart, although some companies serve both. Check the actual reporting location before applying.`}],beginnerTips:[`Start with the Baton Rouge Film Commission's 'Be an Extra' page — it lists the casting companies currently serving the region.`,`Create a free profile with My Casting File, which the film commission lists first among its casting resources.`,`When a call goes out, submit exactly what is requested: recent unfiltered photos, accurate measurements, and your real availability.`],localConsiderations:[`Baton Rouge work comes in waves tied to individual productions. Long quiet stretches between features are normal.`,`Some Louisiana casting companies serve the whole state. Confirm whether a notice reports in Baton Rouge, New Orleans, or elsewhere.`,`Minors need a parent or guardian involved, and productions set specific rules for child performers — read each call carefully.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Baton Rouge Film Commission — Be an Extra`,description:`Official city film commission page listing the casting companies that serve the capital region, with the explicit note that the commission itself does not cast.`,url:`https://www.filmbatonrouge.com/the-baton-rouge-film-commission/get-started/be-an-extra`,scope:`Baton Rouge capital region`,evidenceId:`br-beanextra`},{name:`Caballero Casting`,description:`Full-service casting company with offices in New Orleans and Baton Rouge, handling principal and extras casting for features, television, commercials, and music videos.`,url:`https://www.caballerocasting.com/about`,scope:`Baton Rouge and New Orleans`,evidenceId:`br-caballero`},{name:`My Casting File`,description:`Free casting-profile platform listed by the Baton Rouge Film Commission for paid casting opportunities.`,url:`https://www.mycastingfile.com/`,scope:`National; listed for Baton Rouge`,evidenceId:`br-mycastingfile`}],nearby:[{name:`New Orleans`,stateSlug:`louisiana`,slug:`new-orleans`},{name:`Lafayette`,stateSlug:`louisiana`},{name:`Shreveport`,stateSlug:`louisiana`}],faqs:[{q:`How do I become an extra in Baton Rouge?`,a:`The Baton Rouge Film Commission's 'Be an Extra' page lists the casting companies serving the region — My Casting File, Caballero Casting, Coulon Casting, and Central Casting. Register with the companies directly.`},{q:`Does the Baton Rouge Film Commission cast extras?`,a:`No. Its Be an Extra page directs performers to casting companies. Use those companies’ official registration or project-submission instructions.`},{q:`Is Baton Rouge the same market as New Orleans?`,a:`They are separate production centers about 80 miles apart. Some companies, like Caballero Casting, maintain offices in both, but always confirm which city a notice concerns.`},{q:`Do Baton Rouge productions pay background actors?`,a:`Recent local news coverage of a feature casting call published paid rates for adults and minors. Rates are set per production — read each casting call for its own terms.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Baton Rouge?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`portland`,stateSlug:`oregon`,name:`Portland`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Portland`,intro:`Extras Only and Adam & the Backgrounds offer starting points for Portland background performers. Use their official registration and project instructions, prepare current photos and sizes, and check the actual work location before applying.`,overview:[`Extras Only describes itself as the Northwest's longest-established full-service extras casting company, founded in Portland in 1994, with an online searchable talent database. Adam & the Backgrounds, founded by a former Portlandia casting department member, lists background casting credits on dozens of Portland-area features and series.`,`Extras Only’s database and Adam & the Backgrounds’ project-specific calls are different ways to seek consideration. Company credits describe past work, not current openings; check the latest instructions before submitting.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Independent and streaming features`,text:`Adam & the Backgrounds' credit list is heavy on independent and streaming features shot in the Portland area. Credits document past work, not current openings.`},{title:`Television series background`,text:`Portland has hosted multi-season series work, and local casting companies maintain standing databases for exactly this kind of recurring need.`},{title:`Commercials for Northwest brands`,text:`Local casting credits include commercials for major Northwest-headquartered brands. Commercial bookings are short and frequent entry points.`}],beginnerTips:[`Register with Extras Only's online database and follow Adam & the Backgrounds for project-specific calls — the two companies represent different generations of Portland casting.`,`Read Adam & the Backgrounds' public guidance for new extras: being on time, taking direction, and treating the day as a team effort matters more than standing out.`,`Keep expectations realistic — local casting directors are explicit that background work is not a discovery shortcut, but it is a genuine education in how sets run.`],localConsiderations:[`Bookings depend on individual projects and selection. Keep other work commitments and your budget in mind rather than assuming a busy stretch will continue.`,`An Oregon notice may report outside the Portland area. Check the exact address and travel time before accepting.`,`For outdoor work, check the expected conditions and follow the casting team’s wardrobe and preparation instructions. Ask what rain gear or layers are permitted rather than assuming you can add them on set.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Extras Only`,description:`Portland-based extras casting company founded in 1994, with an online searchable database and a long history of Northwest productions.`,url:`https://extrasonly.com/`,scope:`Portland and the Northwest`,evidenceId:`pdx-extrasonly`},{name:`Adam & the Backgrounds`,description:`Portland background casting company founded by a former Portlandia casting department member, with credits on dozens of local features and series.`,url:`https://adamandthebackgrounds.com/about`,scope:`Portland and Oregon`,evidenceId:`pdx-adam`}],nearby:[{name:`Seattle`,stateSlug:`washington`,slug:`seattle`},{name:`Salem`,stateSlug:`oregon`},{name:`Eugene`,stateSlug:`oregon`}],faqs:[{q:`Who casts extras in Portland?`,a:`Extras Only has cast background in the Northwest since 1994, and Adam & the Backgrounds handles background for many Portland-area features and series. Register through each company's own system.`},{q:`How do I apply for Portland extras work?`,a:`Follow Extras Only’s database instructions or Adam & the Backgrounds’ project-specific calls. Read the complete notice for photos, dates, location, and submission details; a profile is not a booking.`},{q:`Is background work a way to get discovered?`,a:`Do not count on background work leading to a speaking role or regular income. It can provide set experience, but future casting depends on each project’s needs and decisions.`},{q:`Is Portland the same market as Seattle?`,a:`No. They are separate markets about three hours apart. Some Northwest companies work in both, but confirm the reporting location before applying.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Portland?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`orlando`,stateSlug:`florida`,name:`Orlando`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Orlando`,intro:`R.J.’s Casting and Heather Heinz Casting describe work in Orlando and the Southeast, including commercials and screen productions. Check for background-specific notices and keep theme park employment separate from per-project extras work.`,overview:[`Start with the casting company’s official performer instructions. A notice may be for commercial talent, a speaking role, or background performers, so read the role description before submitting. Company service descriptions do not establish an open job.`,`R.J.'s Casting is an Orlando-based full-service company specializing in kids, theme parks, live action, print, and extras for commercials and features, with credits spanning major theme parks and national brands. Heather Heinz has cast commercials, TV, film, and print in the Southeast since 1997, including 15 years operating a casting studio on the Universal Orlando backlot.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Commercials and theme park campaigns`,text:`Local casting companies list theme parks, resorts, and brands among their clients. Those credits describe past work, not guaranteed commercial openings.`},{title:`Kids and family casting`,text:`R.J.'s Casting names kids and theme park work among its specialties — a distinctive Orlando category with its own rules for minors.`},{title:`Film and television`,text:`R.J.’s Casting describes extras work for features, and Heather Heinz Casting lists film and television casting. Check each notice for the actual role, dates, and location.`}],beginnerTips:[`Keep recent, accurate photos and clothing sizes ready. Use each company’s current requirements rather than an old application checklist.`,`Follow each company’s official performer process and reply to suitable notices only when you can meet the requested dates and location.`,`If you are under 18, a parent or guardian must be involved, and productions follow specific child-performer rules.`],localConsiderations:[`Theme park work and film work are different worlds. Park entertainment jobs are employment; background casting is per-project. Do not confuse the two.`,`Confirm the required arrival time, reporting address, and expected availability before accepting. Do not arrange travel around an unconfirmed application.`,`Orlando, Tampa, and Miami are separate casting markets. Some companies cover all three, but confirm where a project reports.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`R.J.'s Casting`,description:`Orlando-based full-service casting company specializing in kids, theme parks, live action, print, and extras for commercials and features.`,url:`https://rjscasting.com/`,scope:`Orlando and Florida`,evidenceId:`orl-rjs`},{name:`Heather Heinz Casting`,description:`Southeast casting director since 1997 for commercials, TV, film, and print, formerly operating a casting studio on the Universal Orlando backlot.`,url:`https://www.heatherheinz.com/`,scope:`Orlando and the Southeast`,evidenceId:`orl-heinz`}],nearby:[{name:`Tampa`,stateSlug:`florida`,slug:`tampa`},{name:`Miami`,stateSlug:`florida`,slug:`miami`},{name:`Atlanta`,stateSlug:`georgia`,slug:`atlanta`}],faqs:[{q:`Who casts extras in Orlando?`,a:`R.J.’s Casting describes extras work for commercials and features, and Heather Heinz Casting covers commercials, TV, film, and print. Use each company’s official instructions and check whether a notice is specifically for background performers.`},{q:`Is theme park performing the same as background acting?`,a:`No. Theme park entertainment roles are auditions for employment with the park. Background acting is per-project work through casting companies. Orlando offers plenty of both, but they are separate paths.`},{q:`Does an Orlando company only cast Orlando shoots?`,a:`Not necessarily. Local companies describe wider Florida or Southeast work. Check the reporting address and travel arrangements before applying or accepting.`},{q:`Can kids be extras in Orlando?`,a:`Yes — kids and family casting is an established Orlando specialty, but a parent or guardian must be involved and productions follow child-performer rules. Read each casting call's requirements.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Orlando?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`philadelphia`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`,name:`Philadelphia`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Philadelphia`,intro:`Philadelphia is one of the East Coast's established production cities. The Greater Philadelphia Film Office posts casting calls publicly, and companies like Mike Lemon Casting and Heery Loftus Casting have served the region for decades.`,overview:[`The Greater Philadelphia Film Office, based in City Hall, maintains a public jobs board that has carried background casting calls for feature films and series shooting in the city. It is one of the few film offices that regularly surfaces extras opportunities directly.`,`Mike Lemon Casting serves Greater Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and New York. Heery Loftus Casting’s CAP guidance explains performer profiles, marking availability, and booking messages. Use each company’s official process; creating a profile or marking availability does not mean you are booked.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Prestige television background`,text:`Heery Loftus Casting's credit list includes multiple HBO, Netflix, and Apple TV+ series shot in the Philadelphia region. Series work can mean recurring background needs over a season.`},{title:`Feature films`,text:`Philadelphia has hosted studio features for decades, and the film office's board has carried background calls for local feature productions.`},{title:`Commercials and business videos`,text:`Mike Lemon Casting lists commercials and industrials—videos made for businesses—alongside other services. Read each notice to distinguish background work from speaking, voice-over, or print roles.`}],beginnerTips:[`Watch the Greater Philadelphia Film Office's jobs board — background calls for local productions are posted there with submission instructions.`,`Follow Mike Lemon Casting’s performer instructions and Heery Loftus Casting’s CAP guidance. Keep photos, sizes, and contact details current, and wait for the company’s booking confirmation before treating a date as work.`,`Philadelphia casts for productions across Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and sometimes New York — be clear about how far you can travel when you submit.`],localConsiderations:[`Philadelphia and Pittsburgh are separate markets on opposite ends of the state, with different casting companies and different production communities.`,`Some Philadelphia-area calls are volunteer or deferred-pay indie projects. The film office posts the compensation terms — read them before submitting.`,`The region's casting companies often work across state lines. A 'Philadelphia' company may cast a project filming in New Jersey.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Greater Philadelphia Film Office — Jobs Board`,description:`Official film office board posting local casting calls and crew openings, including background opportunities for Philadelphia productions.`,url:`https://film.org/job/`,scope:`Greater Philadelphia`,evidenceId:`phl-gpfo`},{name:`Mike Lemon Casting`,description:`Casting company serving Greater Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and New York. Use its official performer instructions and suitable project notices.`,url:`https://mikelemoncasting.com/`,scope:`Greater Philadelphia and the tri-state area`,evidenceId:`phl-lemon`},{name:`Heery Loftus Casting — How CAP Works`,description:`Official performer guidance for the free Casting Access Portal: creating a profile, marking availability, and responding to booking requests. Availability is consideration, not a confirmed booking.`,url:`https://www.castinghl.com/new-page-2`,scope:`Philadelphia, New Jersey, and New York`,evidenceId:`phl-heery-cap`}],nearby:[{name:`Pittsburgh`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`,slug:`pittsburgh`},{name:`New York City`,stateSlug:`new-york`,slug:`new-york-city`},{name:`Wilmington, DE`,stateSlug:`pennsylvania`}],faqs:[{q:`How do I find Philadelphia casting calls?`,a:`The Greater Philadelphia Film Office posts casting calls on its public jobs board, including background opportunities. Local casting companies like Mike Lemon Casting also maintain talent databases.`},{q:`Who casts background actors in Philadelphia?`,a:`Mike Lemon Casting and Heery Loftus Casting are among the established companies serving the region, and individual productions post calls through the film office.`},{q:`Are all Philadelphia casting calls paid?`,a:`No. The film office's board has carried both paid calls and volunteer or deferred-pay independent projects. Compensation is listed in each posting — read it before submitting.`},{q:`Is Philadelphia the same market as Pittsburgh?`,a:`No. They are separate production communities about 300 miles apart with different casting companies. Confirm which city a Pennsylvania notice concerns.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Philadelphia?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`charlotte`,stateSlug:`north-carolina`,name:`Charlotte`,published:!0,headline:`Becoming an Extra in Charlotte`,intro:`C&J Casting and the North Carolina Film Office’s productions page offer starting points for researching Charlotte-area work. Check which projects name a background casting contact, then follow that contact’s latest instructions.`,overview:[`The North Carolina Film Office’s productions page organizes projects by region and may include background casting information. Look for a Charlotte-region project with a named casting contact; a production listing alone is not an open application.`,`C&J Casting is based in Charlotte and lists film, television, commercial, and industrial credits across the Southeast. Local news has also documented Tona B. Dahlquist Casting recruiting background performers for Charlotte features. Past recruitment does not establish a current opening.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Feature-film background`,text:`Dated local news has documented paid extras recruitment for Charlotte features. For applications, use a current notice from the named casting company rather than an old news story.`},{title:`Television series`,text:`The state film office's productions page has listed Charlotte-region series with background opportunities. Series work can provide recurring days over a season.`},{title:`Commercials and business videos`,text:`C&J Casting’s credits include commercials, industrials (videos for businesses), and infomercials. Those categories can involve different roles; check whether a notice requests background performers.`}],beginnerTips:[`Check the North Carolina film office's current-productions page for Charlotte-region projects, then find the casting company each production names.`,`Register with Charlotte-based casting companies before you need them — when a big feature comes to town, calls move fast.`,`Follow submission formats exactly: Charlotte casting calls have specified subject-line formats, photo requirements, and measurement details.`],localConsiderations:[`Charlotte and Wilmington are North Carolina's two production centers, about 200 miles apart. Statewide notices may concern either — check the region listed.`,`Check each notice’s filming dates and required availability before applying. A profile or submission does not guarantee work, even when a production is listed locally.`,`Charlotte's growth means traffic and sprawl are real factors. Confirm the reporting location and plan travel time before accepting a booking.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`C&J Casting`,description:`Charlotte-based casting directors for the Southeast, with feature, television, commercial, and industrial credits.`,url:`https://cjcasting.com/`,scope:`Charlotte and the Southeast`,evidenceId:`clt-cj`},{name:`North Carolina Film Office — Current Productions`,description:`State film office page listing active productions by region, including background and extras opportunities for Charlotte-area projects.`,url:`https://www.filmnc.com/current-productions`,scope:`Statewide North Carolina, by region`,evidenceId:`clt-filmnc`}],nearby:[{name:`Wilmington`,stateSlug:`north-carolina`,slug:`wilmington`},{name:`Atlanta`,stateSlug:`georgia`,slug:`atlanta`},{name:`Asheville`,stateSlug:`north-carolina`}],faqs:[{q:`Who casts extras in Charlotte?`,a:`C&J Casting is based in Charlotte, and larger productions bring in additional casting companies — local news documented Tona B. Dahlquist Casting handling extras for two studio features. The state film office lists active productions by region.`},{q:`How should I use Charlotte production listings?`,a:`Look for the Charlotte region and a named background casting contact. Then check the casting company’s latest notice for the role, dates, and submission instructions; a listed production does not guarantee an opening.`},{q:`Does a film commission book me as an extra?`,a:`No. Use the casting contact named in the project notice. Registration, submissions, and booking decisions belong to casting companies and productions.`},{q:`Are Charlotte and Wilmington the same market?`,a:`No. They are separate production centers about 200 miles apart. North Carolina's productions page lists projects by region, so check which area a notice concerns.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Charlotte?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site. We do not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`miami`,stateSlug:`florida`,name:`Miami`,published:!0,headline:`Background Acting in Miami`,intro:`Casting TaylorMade’s background calls and Film Miami’s job listings offer starting points for Miami-area performers. Check the role, work dates, and reporting location, then follow the named casting team’s application instructions.`,overview:[`Check Film Miami’s job listings for background-specific notices, then follow the named casting contact’s application instructions. The county office shares information; it does not replace the casting team.`,`Casting TaylorMade identifies Miami among its markets and publishes background casting calls and application/database guidance. Its market presence is not evidence that a role is currently open or that every project films in Miami-Dade.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Project-specific background calls`,text:`Follow official local office announcements or a casting company’s own posted call; check the date, exact location, eligibility, and requested submission materials.`},{title:`Commercial and filmed production work`,text:`Casting TaylorMade describes background casting for film, television and commercials; individual projects determine location and requirements.`}],beginnerTips:[`Use Film Miami’s official job listings as a lead, then verify that a notice is for background performers rather than crew.`,`Use Casting TaylorMade’s official talent/application instructions where relevant; a database entry does not guarantee selection.`,`Keep recent natural head-and-shoulders and full-body photos and accurate measurements ready; follow each notice rather than reusing old instructions.`],localConsiderations:[`Be prepared to travel around the Miami area. Filming locations may be in Miami, Miami Beach, Coral Gables, or other nearby communities.`,`Check the location before accepting a booking. Make sure you can get to the set on time, especially if the production requires an early-morning arrival.`,`Plan for South Florida’s weather. Outdoor filming can involve heat, humidity, and sudden rain, so follow the casting team’s wardrobe and preparation instructions.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Miami-Dade County Office of Film & Entertainment — Film Miami`,description:`Official county production information and job-listing resource; a notice may be project-specific and countywide.`,url:`https://filmiami.org/`,scope:`Miami-Dade County`,evidenceId:`miami-film-office`},{name:`Casting TaylorMade`,description:`Extras casting company whose official site identifies Miami among its markets and offers casting-call and talent application routes; verify the location and date of each notice.`,url:`https://castingtaylormade.com/`,scope:`Miami market and beyond; project locations vary`,evidenceId:`taylor-made-casting`}],nearby:[{name:`Tampa`,stateSlug:`florida`,slug:`tampa`},{name:`Orlando`,stateSlug:`florida`,slug:`orlando`}],faqs:[{q:`Is Film Miami a casting agency?`,a:`Film Miami is the county’s production-support office. Its job listings and announcements are leads; performer applications go to the casting contact named in a suitable notice, not a general film-office talent registry.`},{q:`Can Miami-area bookings require travel beyond the city?`,a:`Yes. A notice may concern Miami Beach, Coral Gables, or another nearby community. Check the exact reporting address and required arrival time before accepting.`},{q:`Does registering with a casting company guarantee work?`,a:`No. Registration or submission only makes you available for consideration; projects determine hiring and reporting details.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers hire or cast extras?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an informational resource, not a casting company or employer.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`tampa`,stateSlug:`florida`,name:`Tampa`,published:!0,headline:`Background Acting in Tampa`,intro:`CROWDshot describes extras casting in Tampa and other Florida markets. Pair its official project instructions with the neighboring St. Pete-Clearwater extras preparation guide, and check which side of Tampa Bay you would need to reach.`,overview:[`Film Tampa Bay’s job information can provide leads, but not every listing is for performers. Look for a background-specific notice and use the named casting team’s submission instructions; the commission is not an extras roster.`,`CROWDshot describes background casting for film, television, and commercials and lists Tampa among its Florida markets. Use the company’s own contact information to ask about a suitable project or its intake process. The neighboring St. Pete-Clearwater film office has a useful extras preparation guide, but it is not a Tampa-specific jobs source.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Background casting leads`,text:`Check a casting company’s direct, current instructions and confirm that its notice actually covers Tampa/Hillsborough and the exact shoot location.`},{title:`Commercial and other productions`,text:`CROWDshot describes film, television, and commercial background casting. Each notice defines the role, dates, and reporting location; company services do not guarantee an opening.`}],beginnerTips:[`Look for a background-specific notice in Film Tampa Bay’s job information or a casting company’s official channels. Check the publication date and work dates before responding.`,`Contact a casting company only through its published official contact route; confirm whether it accepts general talent submissions before sending materials.`,`Prepare recent photos and accurate measurements, and expect projects may request wardrobe you supply; always follow the project notice.`],localConsiderations:[`Tampa/Hillsborough and St. Pete-Clearwater are neighboring production areas, not the same reporting location. Confirm which side of the bay a notice concerns before accepting.`,`Ask about your call time (required arrival time), parking, and reporting address. A casting company’s regional base is not necessarily the filming location.`,`Keep a full day available only when you can meet the project’s stated schedule; the regional extras guide describes waiting and potentially long workdays.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Film Tampa Bay — Tampa Hillsborough Film and Digital Media Commission`,description:`Official Tampa-Hillsborough job information. Look for performer notices and follow the named casting contact; this is not an extras registration service.`,url:`https://filmtampabay.com/`,scope:`Tampa/Hillsborough; check each notice’s location`,evidenceId:`tampa-film-office`},{name:`CROWDshot Casting`,description:`Company describes extras/background casting for film, television, and commercials across Florida markets including Tampa. Ask through its official contact route about current project instructions; no open general signup is assumed.`,url:`https://crowdshot.wixsite.com/crowdshot`,scope:`Company-claimed Florida markets, including Tampa`,evidenceId:`crowdshot-casting`},{name:`St. Pete-Clearwater — Become a Film Extra`,description:`Official neighboring-region guide to photos, measurements, wardrobe, and expectations. Preparation guidance, not a Tampa jobs board.`,url:`https://www.visitstpeteclearwater.com/film/become-film-extra`,scope:`St. Pete-Clearwater; regional preparation guidance`,evidenceId:`st-pete-extra-guidance`}],nearby:[{name:`Miami`,stateSlug:`florida`,slug:`miami`},{name:`Orlando`,stateSlug:`florida`,slug:`orlando`}],faqs:[{q:`Does Film Tampa Bay cast background actors?`,a:`Film Tampa Bay provides production support and industry resources. It is not a standing background-performer registry; applications belong to the casting team named in a notice.`},{q:`Can I submit to CROWDshot for Tampa extras work?`,a:`CROWDshot identifies Tampa among its background-casting markets. Use its official contact route to check the process for a suitable project; do not assume it accepts general registrations without instructions.`},{q:`Could a Tampa Bay booking report outside Tampa?`,a:`Yes. Check whether you would report in Tampa, St. Petersburg, Clearwater, or another location around the bay. Confirm the address and travel time before accepting.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers hire or cast extras?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an informational resource, not a casting company or employer.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`houston`,stateSlug:`texas`,name:`Houston`,published:!0,headline:`Background Acting in Houston`,intro:`Houston-based casting companies offer screen and commercial casting services, while the Texas Film Commission provides statewide performer notices and beginner guidance. Learn to separate a company’s talent-network intake from a project application and check whether the work really reports in the Houston area.`,overview:[`Begin with Texas Film Commission casting calls and its actor guidance. Those are statewide resources; a Texas call may be far from Houston. Its actor page says applications use the email and recent photos specified in each notice, with report details supplied if hired.`,`GS Casting describes film, television, commercial, and branded casting from Houston. Covington Select offers a talent-network intake and describes background services across Texas from Houston headquarters. Follow a verified performer intake or project notice; a company service page is not a job application.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Project-specific background calls`,text:`State Job Hotline notices may include casting calls, but verify location, dates and paid status on the individual current notice before applying.`},{title:`Commercial and screen casting networks`,text:`GS Casting describes commercial, film, television, and branded casting services from Houston. Those service descriptions support categories to investigate, not a promise of available background roles.`}],beginnerTips:[`Check the Texas Job Hotline for current notices and apply only as the notice directs; use current photos and accurate contact details.`,`If hired, confirm pay and work dates in a written deal memo (work agreement) or contract, as the Texas Film Commission advises.`,`Treat talent-network registration as profile submission, not guaranteed consideration or employment.`],localConsiderations:[`A Houston-based company can cast projects elsewhere in Texas. Check each notice’s actual reporting location rather than using the company’s home base as the work location.`,`Confirm the reporting address, call time (required arrival time), parking or transit instructions, and whether you must arrange your own travel and lodging before accepting.`,`The Texas Film Commission’s directory of extras casting directors is a directory resource, not an active-job list.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Texas Film Commission — Casting Calls`,description:`Official statewide casting-call landing page; filter each notice for Houston-area location and current dates.`,url:`https://gov.texas.gov/film/hotline/casting`,scope:`Statewide Texas; locations vary`,evidenceId:`TX_CASTING`},{name:`Texas Film Commission — Getting Started as an Actor`,description:`Official guidance on background work, applying to a Job Hotline notice, and written pay/date terms.`,url:`https://gov.texas.gov/film/page/filming_extras`,scope:`Statewide Texas`,evidenceId:`TX_ACTOR`},{name:`GS Casting`,description:`Houston-based casting company describing film, TV, and commercial services across Texas. Check its official performer or project instructions before sending materials; no open general extras signup is established.`,url:`https://gscasting.com/`,scope:`Houston base; statewide service`,evidenceId:`GS_CASTING`},{name:`Covington Select — Join Talent Network`,description:`Company describes talent/background network intake and Texas-wide service from Houston headquarters; no booking promise.`,url:`https://covingtonselectcasting.com/`,scope:`Houston HQ; statewide`,evidenceId:`COVINGTON`}],nearby:[{name:`San Antonio`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`san-antonio`},{name:`Austin`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`austin`}],faqs:[{q:`Where should I look for Houston background work?`,a:`Start with the Texas Film Commission casting-call page and filter notices for a real Houston-area work location and dates. Its listings are statewide, not Houston-specific.`},{q:`Can registering with a casting company guarantee Houston work?`,a:`No. Public company pages describe services or network profiles, not a booking or current opening. Follow project-specific instructions only.`},{q:`What should I confirm before accepting a Houston booking?`,a:`Confirm the reporting address, call time, parking or transportation instructions, and written pay and work dates. A company based in Houston may be casting a project elsewhere in Texas.`},{q:`Are Texas film-office casting calls Houston-only?`,a:`No. The board covers Texas. Check the location and dates in each notice and distinguish performer calls from crew or other production jobs.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers hire extras?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational guide and does not cast, hire or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`san-antonio`,stateSlug:`texas`,name:`San Antonio`,published:!0,headline:`Background Acting in San Antonio`,intro:`For San Antonio background work, start with Texas Film Commission casting notices and actor guidance. Check the actual filming location and follow the named casting team’s application instructions; a company’s local service page is not a booking.`,overview:[`Film San Antonio helps projects share cast and crew calls, but its page is for project owners—not a performer signup. For an extras application, use a published notice’s casting contact and requested materials.`,`The Texas Film Commission’s Casting Calls board and Getting Started as an Actor guide are performer-focused resources. Covington Select describes a talent network serving Texas from Houston; check its current intake instructions rather than assuming a San Antonio service page accepts applications.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`San Antonio-area background notices`,text:`Look for a project notice that names background roles, work dates, the reporting area, and a casting contact. Apply through that contact only when the requirements fit you.`},{title:`Statewide Texas notices`,text:`Texas Film Commission calls can occur anywhere in the state; apply only when the location and timing work for you.`},{title:`Commercial and production casting`,text:`Local-market service pages describe company capabilities, not open jobs. Do not treat a directory/profile form as an extras vacancy.`}],beginnerTips:[`Check city-promoted calls and state Job Hotline notices; confirm each deadline, location, compensation and submission contact.`,`Prepare recent photos and accurate contact details, then submit only the materials requested in the notice. A city project-promotion form is not a performer application.`,`Use only free application/audition routes; the city states calls it promotes must be free and open to the public.`],localConsiderations:[`A San Antonio-area booking may report beyond the city itself. Check the exact address and whether you can arrive on time before accepting.`,`Check the performer application deadline and work dates in the actual notice. Apply only when you can meet the schedule.`,`A San Antonio landing page does not prove a local office or active role; Covington states its Texas markets are served from Houston headquarters.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Texas Film Commission — Casting Calls`,description:`Statewide public casting-call page; filter individual calls by actual location and dates.`,url:`https://gov.texas.gov/film/hotline/casting`,scope:`Statewide Texas`,evidenceId:`TX_CASTING`},{name:`Texas Film Commission — Getting Started as an Actor`,description:`Official background-actor application guidance and written pay/date terms.`,url:`https://gov.texas.gov/film/page/filming_extras`,scope:`Statewide Texas`,evidenceId:`TX_ACTOR`},{name:`Covington Select — San Antonio`,description:`Company describes San Antonio service from Houston headquarters. This market page is not an extras application; use the company’s verified talent-network instructions or a suitable project notice.`,url:`https://covingtonselectcasting.com/casting-agency-san-antonio`,scope:`San Antonio market; Houston HQ`,evidenceId:`COVINGTON_SA`}],nearby:[{name:`Houston`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`houston`},{name:`Austin`,stateSlug:`texas`,slug:`austin`}],faqs:[{q:`Does Film San Antonio accept performer applications?`,a:`Its Cast & Crew Calls page describes project owners submitting eligible calls for city promotion. It is not a general actor-registration or extras application page.`},{q:`What should I check about a San Antonio-area location?`,a:`Confirm the exact reporting address, required arrival time, parking or transit directions, and any local-hire terms. A regional label does not tell you where you would report.`},{q:`Are San Antonio casting company pages current job listings?`,a:`No. Company service and market pages do not establish an active opening. Look for a dated project call with explicit submission instructions.`},{q:`Can a city-promoted call charge for applying or auditioning?`,a:`Film San Antonio says calls in its promotion program must have free applications and auditions open to the public. That is a rule for the city program, not a certification of every advertisement elsewhere.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational guide and does not cast, hire or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`},{slug:`detroit`,stateSlug:`michigan`,name:`Detroit`,published:!0,headline:`Background Acting in Detroit`,intro:`Real Style’s official talent portal and Detroit-based Carrie Ray Casting offer starting points for researching local screen work. Check whether a notice is for background performers and confirm its metro-area location before applying.`,overview:[`Real Style Talent describes extras, commercial talent, and actors among its Midwest services, with film, television, and commercial work in its portfolio. Its official talent portal offers profile creation. A profile makes your information available for consideration; it does not establish an open role or guarantee a booking.`,`Carrie Ray Casting identifies Detroit as its base and describes union and non-union work across film, television, commercials, business videos, and real-people casting. That wider casting practice is not a background-only signup. Follow each company’s own instructions for a suitable project.`,`For background applications, use a casting company’s official talent portal or the contact in a suitable project notice. Detroit’s city film office does not place performers in jobs. Keep your application materials focused on the casting team’s requirements.`],opportunityTypes:[{title:`Screen-production extras`,text:`Real Style describes extras talent and prior film and television work. Investigate project-specific background notices; a service portfolio is not a schedule of available jobs.`},{title:`Commercial talent and everyday portrayals`,text:`Real Style and Carrie Ray Casting describe commercial and actor casting. Check whether a notice requests non-speaking background, speaking performers, or real-people talent rather than treating the categories as interchangeable.`}],beginnerTips:[`Use Real Style’s official talent portal for its current profile requirements. Read its terms before sharing information; no fee policy or promise of work is assumed.`,`Keep recent natural photos, truthful measurements, and reliable contact information ready. Follow the specific notice’s requested materials and availability.`,`Confirm that a call is for background performers and check its work location and dates. A Detroit casting company may serve a wider region.`],localConsiderations:[`A Detroit-area booking may report outside the city. Confirm the exact address, parking, and transportation before committing.`,`Ask about your call time (required arrival time), wardrobe, expected availability, and written work terms before accepting. Do not arrange travel around an unconfirmed submission.`,`Use Real Style’s official talent portal for profile registration. Follow its current requirements and share personal information only through the verified process.`],localCastingResources:[{name:`Real Style Talent — Talent Signup`,description:`Official Michigan talent-profile portal linked to Real Style’s extras and commercial-talent services. Check current requirements and terms; creating a profile does not guarantee work.`,url:`https://talent.realstyleonline.com/signup`,scope:`Michigan/Midwest talent network; project locations vary`,evidenceId:`p4-realstyle-signup`},{name:`Carrie Ray Casting`,description:`Detroit-based casting director describing film, television, commercials, business videos, and real-people work. Follow a suitable project’s performer instructions; a general extras signup is not established.`,url:`https://www.carrieraycasting.com/experience/`,scope:`Detroit-based; project scope varies`,evidenceId:`p4-carrieray`}],nearby:[{name:`Cleveland`,stateSlug:`ohio`,slug:`cleveland`},{name:`Chicago`,stateSlug:`illinois`,slug:`chicago`}],faqs:[{q:`Does Detroit’s film office cast extras?`,a:`No. The city says its film office does not provide employment placement. Use the casting company’s official performer instructions or the contact in a suitable project notice instead.`},{q:`How do I submit for Detroit background work?`,a:`Real Style provides an official talent-profile portal for Michigan talent, including extras. Check its current requirements and follow any suitable project’s application instructions; registration is not a booking.`},{q:`Is every local casting notice an extras role?`,a:`No. Detroit-based casting services include commercials, speaking roles, real-people casting, and other categories. Read the role description and submit only for work you are eligible and available to do.`},{q:`Is a Michigan film-office notice necessarily in Detroit?`,a:`No. Statewide resources apply across Michigan; verify the location and reporting instructions in each project notice.`},{q:`Does Scene Seekers book extras in Detroit?`,a:`No. Scene Seekers is an independent informational site and does not cast, hire, or represent performers.`}],lastUpdated:`2026-10-28`}],t=e.filter(e=>e.published);function n(t,n){return e.find(e=>e.stateSlug===t&&e.slug===n&&e.published)}export{n,t};